should you work with non ideal customers  this is going to be a problem that you  face in any business that you start  you're going to have the customers who  love what you do who get the value that  you provide and are willing to pay you  what you're worth and then you're going  to get other customers who like your  service like your product I willing to  pay you a certain amount but they're  never going to be ideal customers and  that's going to be most of your  customers at the start they're people  who they don't quite get it you know  they're not they're very price conscious  like if you were to increase your price  by ten percent they're gone that's not  an ideal customer for you so the  challenge for how to how to work with  ideal customers for me depends on what  stage you're at in your business ok this  question comes as a result of somebody  writing me a question this was from my  newsletter reader EO EG oma Wow hope I  pronounced that right sorry for the  pronunciation there basically she has a  dress company she designs dresses and  fabrics for people but ninety percent of  the people come into her are not ideal  customers she doesn't know what to do  the problem here is it will really  depend on what phase you're right in  your business for me what i recommend  entrepreneur's doing the first thing you  need to focus on is getting past  survival getting to the point where you  have enough money to put food on the  table and pay your bills i have a whole  set of guides that help you do that but  you have to get past survival because  it's great to have the big vision the  big idea i want that for you but if if  you run out of money you can't support  you know your mortgage payment or your  rent or pay your electricity bill you're  going to go back to get a job so step  number one is get to survival whatever  that takes how much does that mean for  you and that's not living luxuriously  its survival okay means I don't have to  get a job that's goal number one  and so that means working with less than  ideal customers and the question should  you would you rather work with less than  ideal customers or would you rather be  at a job for most people they pick  running your own business but with less  than ideal customers okay you have to  make a judgment call with each person I  remember an example when I was starting  my business I had a I was growing okay  like the for Evan Carmichael calm I was  seeing traction and I got an offer from  a big computer company I won't say the  name doesn't matter and they basically  wanted me to be a pitchman for their  company and saying we want you to go out  and say how great our company is and  tell everybody on your list and on  social media you tell everybody about  how great we are and that they need to  buy our product and they were throwing a  lot of money at me like wow this is a  lot of cash but it just it did make me  feel good you know like it was too far  it violated my belief system because I  like sharing stuff with you guys that I  use that I thought I believe in that I  think you can get value from I don't  want to say you need to go buy this  computer because it's the best computer  in the world if I'm not using it and I  don't like their product and so I had to  say no to that even though it meant  giving up a big chunk of cash and that  was that was hard but I believe that  there were better opportunities on the  horizon so there is a little bit of a  line you have to walk I would say don't  take on a customer who makes you do  something that goes against what you  believe in okay if they are making you  do something that's against your values  then they're not a good customer for you  okay that's a bad customer then you're  going to have good customers and then  you're going to have great or ideal  customers and a lot of times your  business will start with a lot of good  customers and their frustrating and they  don't get your value but what they do is  they help get you to that point of  survival and once you pass survival  you can leave them and focus on the  better clients and then you can afford  to be more selective and more picky and  hold out for the really good clients the  ideal clients and in that process you  get better at what you do right while  you're working with the good clients you  get more skilled you learn how to  deliver more value because by helping  them you are getting better yourself and  then you have more to bring to an ideal  customer to a great customer so to  summarize my advice ignore the bad  customers if they make you turn in your  stomach and you go to sleep not happy  and you're fighting your beliefs ignore  them they are not worth it for any price  keep the good customers who will get you  to your poorer survival and then start  focusing on the great ideal customers  believe for those of you watching like  the video please give it a thumbs up  below subscribe to the channel if if you  want to see more videos like this and  let me know you think leave a question  below ask me a question about your  business let me know you thought of this  video I'll make a video response thank  you so much and I'll see you soon
 

